<title>USA: USDA offers South Africa $50 mln under GSM-103.</title>
<headline>USDA offers South Africa $50 mln under GSM-103.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Tuesday authorized $50 million in credit guarantees for sales of U.S. farm goods to South Africa under the Intermediate Export Credit Guarantee Program (GSM-103) for fiscal year 1997.</p>
<p>USDA said the commodities covered are barley malt, feed grains, oilseeds, protein meals, vegetable oils, wheat and breeder livestock.</p>
<p>It said sales must be registered by Sept. 30, 1997, with exports no later than Nov. 30, 1997.</p>
</text>
